{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free","id":1055267,"title":"Who set the Solars free?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-26T09:08:43-08:00","id":1055267,"title":"Who set the Solars free?","content":"I'm sure it says somewhere in the book who broke the Jade Prison and freed the Solars, but for the life of me I can't find it. So, as the title reads, who freed the Solars and why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10179-shadryx","name":"shadryx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T09:15:07-08:00","id":1055272,"title":"","content":"I did, it was a busy week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T09:25:53-08:00","id":1055276,"title":"","content":"It was the Deathlords. They were trying to capture them all for Project: Abyssal but only managed to get about half of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T09:32:27-08:00","id":1055278,"title":"","content":"In 1st and 2nd edition, it was the Deathlords. With assistance from the Yozi, they built a gigantic undead behemoth/hekatonkhire and shattered the Jade Prison. It was supposed to capture all of the Solar Exaltations, but only managed to capture half of them. Then the Deathlords gave 50 Exaltations to the Yozi in exchange for the assistance. <br /> <br /> However, that was only true of the older editions. While it's likely that 3rd edition will stick to this, it's possible that there will be some divergences as well, so feel free to use it, or not, for your own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T09:32:57-08:00","id":1055279,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadryx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free#post1055267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure it says somewhere in the book who broke the Jade Prison and freed the Solars, but for the life of me I can't find it. So, as the title reads, who freed the Solars and why?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if it's exactly the same as it was in the first two editions, but here goes:<br /> <br /> The Deathlords and the Yozis struck a deal: The Deathlords, who weren't utterly barred from Creation, would break open the Jade Prison and capture the Solar Exaltations. In exchange for part of the haul, the Yozis would teach the Deathlords how to contain and alter the Exaltations.<br /> <br /> That's how we got Abyssals and Infernals, too.<br /> <br /> Fortunately for everyone who wasn't involved, the giant necro-beast the Deathlords created and sent after the Jade Prison didn't work entirely as intended: the monster was able to break it open, but a goodly number of the Solar Exaltations escaped.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T09:58:46-08:00","id":1055295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055278#post1055278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 1st and 2nd edition, it was the Deathlords. With assistance from the Yozi, they built a gigantic undead behemoth/hekatonkhire and shattered the Jade Prison. It was supposed to capture all of the Solar Exaltations, but only managed to capture half of them. Then the Deathlords gave 50 Exaltations to the Yozi in exchange for the assistance.<br /> <br /> However, that was only true of the older editions. While it's likely that 3rd edition will stick to this, it's possible that there will be some divergences as well, so feel free to use it, or not, for your own games.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the most true statement on here, with the possible exception of the Yozi gaining 50 of them in 1e. Not sure on that one, since Infernals never got their own splat in 1e.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, all true, especially what was said for 3e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T12:00:41-08:00","id":1055331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shadryx</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm sure it says somewhere in the book who broke the Jade Prison and freed the Solars, but for the life of me I can't find it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is not mentioned in the Third Edition core.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055278#post1055278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While it's likely that 3rd edition will stick to this</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b{intended with tone of genuine curiosity rather than confrontation} Why do you think that is?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T12:11:26-08:00","id":1055339,"title":"","content":"What did the Jadeprison look like? <br /> <br /> What did the exaltations look live? <br /> (When they still were in the Jadeprison)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1887-colognian","name":"Colognian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T12:28:55-08:00","id":1055346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055331#post1055331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200b{intended with tone of genuine curiosity rather than confrontation} Why do you think that is?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the origin of the Abyssals and Infernals is being changed drastically, keeping the same explanation is the easiest way to explain both their origins and why the solars are now out.<br /> <br /> It's not impossible to change, but it could shake up the very nature of two splats.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I thank the Devs for the great game of Exalted!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12735-bjornthefellhanded","name":"BjornTheFellhanded","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12735_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"327"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T12:39:00-08:00","id":1055348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055331#post1055331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b{intended with tone of genuine curiosity rather than confrontation} Why do you think that is?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the Abyssal/Infernal Kickstarter previews -<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Abyssal Kickstarter -<br /> Further, it led many to believe it would be better to just erase the connection between Solars and Abyssals and start over.<br /> <br /> However, I want to follow the intentions that went behind the making of the Abyssals and fully realize those intentions, making good on the unspoken promise of long ago. I want to give the players their dark Solars: glorious and deathly champions rocking Solar arete and wielding all the powers of the grave.<br /> <br /> To do that, I need to preserve continuity between Abyssal and Solar Charms. Ergo, the Abyssals are built on a base of Charms identical to many in the Solar set. This establishes them as Solars. The harder part has always been establishing them as something else.<br /> <br /> Infernal Kickstarter -<br /> The Green Sun Princes are the sultans of Hell, devil rajahs uplifted by the Yozis and set loose upon Creation as a plague on the world. As they are uplifted using stolen, tainted Solar Exaltations, their Solar legacy weighs heavily on the Yozi agenda. </div> </div> </div>Morke rejected the idea of simply making Abyssals something <i>else</i> that had nothing to do with Solar Exalted. Instead, he felt that preserving them as &quot;Corrupted Solars&quot; was integral to their concept. So it seems to me that the Deathlords will still have ~100 corrupt Solar Exaltations in 3rd edition and certainly the Infernal kickstarter directly calls Infernal Exalted out as corrupted Solar Exaltations.<br /> <br /> The authors could, of course, come up with an entirely different method by which the Jade Prison was broken, but they would still have to explain how the Deathlords and Yozi were able to capture escaping Solar Exaltations. Any such explanation would necessarily be fairly convoluted, and I'm not sure it would add anything of value to the game if the end result is still going to be about the same, with the Deathlords and Yozi getting access to Solar Exaltations.<br /> <br /> They could also say Infernals and Abyssals have nothing to do with Solar Exaltations and are something new (everything in the previews was noted as being subject to change), but Morke felt fairly strongly about some of these design points so that seems ulikely.<br /> <br /> In the end, &quot;The Deathlords had something to do with the Jade Prison breaking and snagged some Exaltations in the process,&quot; is probably going to continue to be the explanation for Abyssals and Infernals, rather than the authors trying to come up with some convoluted explanation that ends up with everything basically in the same place it was in the earlier editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T12:54:05-08:00","id":1055353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055295#post1055295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is the most true statement on here, with the possible exception of the Yozi gaining 50 of them in 1e. Not sure on that one, since Infernals never got their own splat in 1e.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, all true, especially what was said for 3e.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 50 were very much in first edition. They were going to be used for 'something', and it wasn't quite clear whether they would be Exalted themselves, or just a power source for something else.<br /> <br /> *Grumbles about the fact 1st Ed. seems to be all but forgotten.*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T12:56:46-08:00","id":1055356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055353#post1055353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The 50 were very much in first edition. They were going to be used for 'something', and it wasn't quite clear whether they would be Exalted themselves, or just a power source for something else.<br /> <br /> *Grumbles about the fact 1st Ed. seems to be all but forgotten.*</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know! I played 1e, but I never owned any of the books so I was unfamiliar with some of the metaplot and such. Thanks for the clarification!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T13:20:25-08:00","id":1055363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055348#post1055348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From the Abyssal/Infernal Kickstarter previews -</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe Exaltations being stolen doesn't necessitate that the Deathlords were the ones responsible for the return of the Solars.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy read on various details and the general tone of John is that the Solars return for... whatever reason (possibly by the will of the Unconquered Sun), and then the Deathlords and Yozis hitch their wagons to that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, &quot;The Deathlords had something to do with the Jade Prison breaking and snagged some Exaltations in the process,&quot; is probably going to continue to be the explanation for Abyssals and Infernals, rather than the authors trying to come up with some convoluted explanation that ends up with everything basically in the same place it was in the earlier editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAt the moment, I think that the strongest possibility is that an explanation for the Abyssals and Infernals won't be given at all.<br /> <br /> Sure, they'll probably still be described as stolen and repurposed Essences of the Solar Exalted. Just... no origin story. They exist without overt explanation.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe corebook gets by without explaining how the Solars came back, so I think it's unnecessary to do something defining the transition into Abyssal and Infernal Exalted.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T13:55:48-08:00","id":1055376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055363#post1055363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bAt the moment, I think that the strongest possibility is that an explanation for the Abyssals and Infernals won't be given at all.<br /> <br /> Sure, they'll probably still be described as stolen and repurposed Essences of the Solar Exalted. Just... no origin story. They exist without overt explanation.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe corebook gets by without explaining how the Solars came back, so I think it's unnecessary to do something defining the transition into Abyssal and Infernal Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the least I believe that if we <i>do</i> get an explanation on how the Deathlords and Yozi managed to acquire so many Solar Exaltations, it'll be very close to the one we got back in 1st and 2nd edition, since any other explanation would simply end up being even more convoluted to no real gain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:42:06-08:00","id":1055395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055376#post1055376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At the least I believe that if we <i>do</i> get an explanation on how the Deathlords and Yozi managed to acquire so many Solar Exaltations, it'll be very close to the one we got back in 1st and 2nd edition, since any other explanation would simply end up being even more convoluted to no real gain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Giant crab monster and all? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:46:24-08:00","id":1055397,"title":"","content":"It might also be worth noting that there are hints that the Green Lady had some hand in helping the Deathlords in their plan. My assumption was always that she introduced flaws that caused the Deathlords to fail to trap all of the Exaltations, thereby freeing a bunch of Solars along with giving the Deathlords enough Exaltations to keep them happy. After all, I don't know that anyone except a ranking Sidereal would even know where the Jade Prison was. It also seems to me like the kind of plan that she'd be into, where she helps the Deathlords and Creation, wheels within wheels, playing both sides, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11685-sundance","name":"Sundance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T14:51:07-08:00","id":1055399,"title":"","content":"I SET THE SOLARS FREE!!!!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you think nobody cares if you're alive, try missing a couple of payments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2890-walker-of-ebony-clouds","name":"Walker-of-Ebony-Clouds","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T15:04:50-08:00","id":1055404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055395#post1055395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giant crab monster and all? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this time maybe it'll be a giant Mantis Shrimp. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T15:54:12-08:00","id":1055426,"title":"","content":"I mean, to say that an alternative explanation would have to be convoluted... that implies to me assuming an explanation based on elaboration rather than ambiguity. If an origin had to be given at all, I think the minimum that would be necessary was either that the Deathlords had a mysterious insight forewarning them or acted fairly quickly afterwards, and did something big and scary in the Labyrinth that drew some of the Essences to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T17:31:17-08:00","id":1055463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055426#post1055426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, to say that an alternative explanation would have to be convoluted... that implies to me assuming an explanation based on elaboration rather than ambiguity. If an origin had to be given at all, I think the minimum that would be necessary was either that the Deathlords had a mysterious insight forewarning them or acted fairly quickly afterwards, and did something big and scary in the Labyrinth that drew some of the Essences to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally speaking, for my own piece of mind I don't approach 3rd edition from the point of view that, &quot;Nothing in 1st or 2nd edition applies unless it is directly stated to apply in the books.&quot; For example, even though Paragon doesn't get mentioned in the 3rd edition book (outside of appearing on the world map), I assume that the city is still pretty much like how it was presented in 1st and 2nd edition - ruled by a human with an artifact staff who can magically enforce oaths and who pays tribute to the Scarlet Empress and all that jazz, at least until such a time as we get something saying that the city is completely different.<br /> <br /> In this particular scenario, the end result is identical to how things were in 1st and 2nd edition: the Solars were trapped in the Jade Prison. It broke. The Deathlords managed to get a bunch, and the Yozi got rather less. <br /> <br /> As a result, I'm going to assume things played out fairly similarly in 3rd edition to how they did in previous editions, with the Deathlords having some responsibility for what happened (even if the specifics may have played out somewhat differently) at least until we get information in the books saying that the events regarding the breaking of the Jade Prison <i>are</i> completely different. So far I haven't seen anything that really suggests that's the case, though if I'm wrong though and the the devs or the authors and have said things went down differently and I'm operating on unfounded ideas, by all means let me know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T18:38:54-08:00","id":1055493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055463#post1055463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally speaking, for my own piece of mind I don't approach 3rd edition from the point of view that, &quot;Nothing in 1st or 2nd edition applies unless it is directly stated to apply in the books.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that's not what he said.<br /> <br /> \u200bPart of the point of even <i>having </i>a third edition at all was in allowing there to be some mystique to the setting again. It's not that First or Second Edition no longer apply (especially since the devs have already gone on the record as saying that <i>Scavenger Sons</i> and <i>Games of Divinity</i> are great source material), it's that they don't <i>have</i> to, because, frankly, a lot of their explanations of things kinda sucked in retrospect.<br /> <br /> \u200b(Indeed, as far as my preferences go, this particular presentation, where the only reason the Deathlords' plan didn't result in them getting ALL the power pellets was because their Giant Enemy Crab fucked up and hit the cage too hard, Just As Planned by the Ebon Dragon, is near the top of my list of sucky explanations.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 02-26-2017, 09:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T18:54:21-08:00","id":1055500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055493#post1055493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure that's not what he said.<br /> <br /> \u200bPart of the point of even having a third edition was in allowing there to be some mystique to the setting again. It's not that First or Second Edition no longer apply (especially since the devs have already gone on the record as saying that <i>Scavenger Sons</i> and <i>Games of Divinity</i> are great source material), it's that they don't <i>have</i> to, because, frankly, a lot of their explanations of things kinda sucked in retrospect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isator asked why I thought 3rd edition was likely to have the same explanation for how the Jade Prison was broken and the Deathlords and Yozi acquired their Exaltations, rather than try to conjure up with an entirely new explanation to explain the same result. I provided my reasons.<br /> <br /> Now, it's possible the authors could choose to decline to ever provide any explanation whatsoever. But, I believe however that if we <i>do</i> get an official explanation it's likely going to be very similar to the one we had before, with the Deathlords and Yozi working together in some way to break the Jade Prison. Probably not <i>exactly</i> the same (yeah, the crab is pretty stupid, I agree) but pretty close nevertheless.<br /> <br /> It's cool if you disagree with me and you're dead certain we'll never get an explanation or that it'll be different. That's fine. I think only Morke and maybe Holden know for sure what happened and whether they will explain it or not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T20:28:48-08:00","id":1055522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055404#post1055404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, this time maybe it'll be a giant Mantis Shrimp. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And I thought I was the only one who read John's secret file.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T21:21:34-08:00","id":1055529,"title":"","content":"I hadnt thought of this question yet<br /> <br /> Give me a bit, and I can have some options <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-26T22:37:40-08:00","id":1055545,"title":"","content":"If the Solars are released by something else, the Abyssals could simply be a result of the Solar Exaltations spending too much time &quot;dead&quot; (something that was never intended to happen). They were then noticed and exploited by the Deathlords. It seems reasonable to me that blocking the reincarnation of Solar Exaltations could cause them to be tainted with death.<br /> <br /> (This would imply that Infernal forces were able to gain access to some of them by working through the Deathlords and cutting some sort of deal with them.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T01:44:43-08:00","id":1055565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055500#post1055500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (yeah, the crab is pretty stupid, I agree)</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;That is the dumbest piece of necrotech I have ever seen&quot;<br /> &quot;Look, it'll get the job done. If anyone asks, just lie about it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T03:36:28-08:00","id":1055583,"title":"","content":"I once had the idea that the Essences had been tainted, either hy the Great Curse or the built up karma of their actions, and had somehow purged the taint. But such wasmthe darkness released that it gave birth to new Dark Essences. Thus did the Abyssal shards form","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T12:33:23-08:00","id":1055738,"title":"","content":"I'm my current game I'm running with a slightly more philosophical rendition of the Jade prison. <br /> <br /> Essentially, after the usurpation, the devastation wrought left the world's populace largely in despair - the new world order imposed by the Sidereals is the calculated balance of *just* enough turmoil to satisfy the power players and *just* enough insurmountable social structure to keep the lower classes in line. Balancing the world on this fulcrum of despair and hopelessness while rewarding the more avid and aggressive citizens meant that no one was worthy of Sol's love, adoration and - by extension - Exaltation. <br /> <br /> There were always the fringe cases of someone hoping against hope but they were so few and far between in this new world order that a marginally organized Wyld hunt could track them down easily enough and dispatch them in so much pomp and rituals that it would further dissuade the populace from dreaming the impossible dream. <br /> <br /> The rise of the Scarlet Empire was exactly what the Sidereals needed after the devastation wrought by the crusade and contagion; a new state ordered religion that actually <i>prohibited greatness</i> on a spiritual level, the final nail in the coffin to any potential Solar Exalted. All they had to do was let the empires influence expand, and clean up the last remnants of those few dreamers that had slipped through the web of mundanity. Everything was going great for almost eight centuries and then... the unthinkable happened. <br /> <br /> Suddenly the Realm's influence turns inwards, those Sidereals tasked with maintaining the balance in the threshold areas loose the looming threat of a world-spanning empire and the people start to think that maybe things could be better, and the light of hope begins to return to the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(10chars)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2721-elkovash","name":"Elkovash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:35:27-08:00","id":1055791,"title":"","content":".......I'm so phenomenally, unbelievably glad &quot;Give the Sidereals, as a whole, a canonical Deathlord's master plan&quot; isn't 3e's direction for them, near as I can.tell. And that's not a statement I expected to make today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:07:46-08:00","id":1055817,"title":"","content":"IMO 3e is probably not going address it directly.<br /> <br /> Because having a solid answer doesn't add anything to the game, and leaving it undefined grants ST the ability to make up whatever best suits their own story.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh but the deathlords would have to know and they'd share that information with the Abyssals!&quot; Why? Unless the deathlords are cartoon villians revealing plots to captured heroes or deliberately telling the potentially vastly more powerful Abyssals things they don't need to know, there's nothing to be gained from it.<br /> <br /> &quot;How did you get my exaltation then?!? Oh Eye and Seven Black Rabbits That Peer Into The Abyss to Forsake The Chains that Bind.... *deep breath* to the Eternal Stone That Bears No Death?&quot; Again, simply honest answers work well. &quot;I traded a bunch of land to Bob for it. Canny ghost that Bob. No idea how he got it.&quot; or &quot;As part of a convoluted arrangement with forces so dark the living can not bear to hear even the names of the forces uttered!&quot;<br /> <br /> (IMO again) having it defined just gives players(and the STs) a reason to go &quot;Ah-Ha! my super-clever Abyssal clearly KNOWS they were a Solar before, and is therefore doing X!&quot; or &quot;Well, everyone knows Abyssals are inverted Solars, of course X, Y, Z are all true.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:30:54-08:00","id":1055834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055493#post1055493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200b(Indeed, as far as my preferences go, this particular presentation, where the only reason the Deathlords' plan didn't result in them getting ALL the power pellets was because their Giant Enemy Crab fucked up and hit the cage too hard, Just As Planned by the Ebon Dragon, is near the top of my list of sucky explanations.)</div> </div> </div> </div>The only thing that sort of redeems the crab for me is as part of my growing headcanon that Gloam and it's problems are caused by it being directly above the former site of the Jade Prison.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 02-27-2017, 09:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:41:00-08:00","id":1055838,"title":"","content":"Wait Beneath? Not Above?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:53:31-08:00","id":1055841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Odd_Canuck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055817#post1055817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMO 3e is probably not going address it directly.<br /> <br /> Because having a solid answer doesn't add anything to the game, and leaving it undefined grants ST the ability to make up whatever best suits their own story.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh but the deathlords would have to know and they'd share that information with the Abyssals!&quot; Why? Unless the deathlords are cartoon villians revealing plots to captured heroes or deliberately telling the potentially vastly more powerful Abyssals things they don't need to know, there's nothing to be gained from it.<br /> <br /> &quot;How did you get my exaltation then?!? Oh Eye and Seven Black Rabbits That Peer Into The Abyss to Forsake The Chains that Bind.... *deep breath* to the Eternal Stone That Bears No Death?&quot; Again, simply honest answers work well. &quot;I traded a bunch of land to Bob for it. Canny ghost that Bob. No idea how he got it.&quot; or &quot;As part of a convoluted arrangement with forces so dark the living can not bear to hear even the names of the forces uttered!&quot;<br /> <br /> (IMO again) having it defined just gives players(and the STs) a reason to go &quot;Ah-Ha! my super-clever Abyssal clearly KNOWS they were a Solar before, and is therefore doing X!&quot; or &quot;Well, everyone knows Abyssals are inverted Solars, of course X, Y, Z are all true.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with this.<br /> <br /> Much like with the role of the Incarna in the past editions, we should have enough information to extrapolate and create theories - enough points to support the framework of a theory, but not enough that it is spelled out to us. It might be useful to know if the Neverborn somehow came by then, and passed them to the Deathlords, if the Neverborn are less of a force and the Deathlords just got them themselves, somehow, if they got them from an unnamed-or-named third party, etc. But not the exact mechanics of how.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:09:03-08:00","id":1055853,"title":"","content":"I lean toward it being a heroic Solar who was one of the handful reincarnating during the imprisonment, who freed their brethren and brought back the attention of the Unconquered Sun with an act of heroism in which they died in the process (important that they died, because it means they can be an immediate past incarnation for a PC).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-27-2017, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T18:18:47-08:00","id":1055926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055838#post1055838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait Beneath? Not Above?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunate remnant of the sentence I revised where I said the Jade Prison was beneath Gloam. Probably shouldn't post while tired, but these days that'd be not posting at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T18:19:58-08:00","id":1055928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elkovash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055738#post1055738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm my current game I'm running with a slightly more philosophical rendition of the Jade prison.<br /> <br /> Essentially, after the usurpation, the devastation wrought left the world's populace largely in despair - the new world order imposed by the Sidereals is the calculated balance of *just* enough turmoil to satisfy the power players and *just* enough insurmountable social structure to keep the lower classes in line. Balancing the world on this fulcrum of despair and hopelessness while rewarding the more avid and aggressive citizens meant that no one was worthy of Sol's love, adoration and - by extension - Exaltation.<br /> <br /> There were always the fringe cases of someone hoping against hope but they were so few and far between in this new world order that a marginally organized Wyld hunt could track them down easily enough and dispatch them in so much pomp and rituals that it would further dissuade the populace from dreaming the impossible dream.<br /> <br /> The rise of the Scarlet Empire was exactly what the Sidereals needed after the devastation wrought by the crusade and contagion; a new state ordered religion that actually <i>prohibited greatness</i> on a spiritual level, the final nail in the coffin to any potential Solar Exalted. All they had to do was let the empires influence expand, and clean up the last remnants of those few dreamers that had slipped through the web of mundanity. Everything was going great for almost eight centuries and then... the unthinkable happened.<br /> <br /> Suddenly the Realm's influence turns inwards, those Sidereals tasked with maintaining the balance in the threshold areas loose the looming threat of a world-spanning empire and the people start to think that maybe things could be better, and the light of hope begins to return to the world.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I really like this idea! It plays with the indian vedic themes that are already present in the core (like with the shinma and the Raksha). It feels like what you are describing is from Mayahana Buddhism (I think).The term Maya has been translated as 'illusion,' but then it does not concern normal illusion. 'Illusion' does not mean that the world is not real and simply a figment of the human imagination. Maya means that the world is not as it seems; the world that one experiences is misleading as far as its true nature is concerned. M\u0101y\u0101 not only deceives people about the things they think they know; more basically, it limits their knowledge. That is what you are describing.<br /> <br /> or for a more pop culture reference- it is the matrix. Which is basically Immanuel Kant critique of Reason....<br /> <br /> Or- another philosophical bent- Plato! Plato has Socrates describe a group of people who have lived chained to the wall of a cave all of their lives, facing a blank wall. The people watch shadows projected on the wall from objects passing in front of a fire behind them, and give names to these shadows. The shadows are the prisoners' reality. Socrates explains how the philosopher is like a prisoner who is freed from the cave and comes to understand that the shadows on the wall are not reality at all, for he can perceive the true form of reality rather than the manufactured reality that is the shadows seen by the prisoners. The inmates of this place do not even desire to leave their prison; for they know no better life.<br /> <br /> The Jade prison is Plato's Cave.<br /> <br /> thumbs up dude. I like this metaphorical prison much better than a physical one. Kudos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2556-firstaide","name":"Firstaide","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T20:52:43-08:00","id":1055972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055565#post1055565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;That is the dumbest piece of necrotech I have ever seen&quot;<br /> &quot;Look, it'll get the job done. If anyone asks, just lie about it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And thus began one of the greatest conspiracies of the Underworld. Oaths were sworn, alliances forged, blackmail threatened, all to keep secret that fact that one of the greatest victories in the way against heaven was won by something really REALLY stupid. When it came to light that the deathlords had, in fact, constructed a gigantic crab to smash the jade prison - even though they stood on the threshold of victory against the unconquered sun, they just couldn't bring themselves to accept that the crab was part of their legend, and so agreed to give back all the exaltations... and try again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T21:24:45-08:00","id":1055981,"title":"","content":"Btw, been wracking my brain for other ideas on Abyssal origins, and am realizing something. If the Abyssals were free Exaltations like the Solsrs, this would be easier. But them serving the Deathlords kinda makes it harder to come up with ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:33:38-08:00","id":1056192,"title":"","content":"I am not sure if they are keeping the Deathlords+Yozi stole/released the Solar Exaltations part but I do remember a while back (see years ago) one of the Devs, Holden I think, said that they are changing things so that the Yozi asked for Exactly 50 Solar Exaltations from the Deathlords. He then went on to ask us to consider just why they asked specificially 50 exaltations. <br /> <br /> OFC the whole thing derailed into people asking things like if Infernals are now 100% Evil past lives and others saying that it would be funny if they asked for all the &quot;Good&quot; Solars etc, but there is a definite Deal between the Yozi and the Deathlords for the acquisition of Solar Exaltations. <br /> <br /> OFC this was years ago and may no longer be true but that is the &quot;Latest&quot; info I have on this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2626-yzarc","name":"Yzarc","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2626_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:09:34-08:00","id":1056224,"title":"","content":"Not a single &quot;IT'S ME AUSTIN&quot; in three pages? For shame.<br /> <br /> Anyways, my position is &quot;Deathlords &amp; Yozis is likely but other explanations are not barred at this point&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:19:03-08:00","id":1056228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056224#post1056224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a single &quot;IT'S ME AUSTIN&quot; in three pages?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> was the first to say &quot;it's me,&quot; and any of these types of &quot;silly&quot; replies after the first rapidly become tiresome to slog through.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:28:18-08:00","id":1056239,"title":"","content":"I'd just as soon see it being something totally different that broke the Solars free, regardless of it's narrative impact on the Deathlords and Yozi's getting their hands on some of them. <br /> <br /> I'd love to see the Bronze Sids do it by accident when checking in on it.<br /> I'd love to see the Gold Sids do it intentionally because enough is enough.<br /> I'd love to see the Scarlet Empress do it intentionally when she foresaw a massive threat in the near future.<br /> I'd love to see the Lunars do it by accident, when they think they're assaulting the Scarlet Empress' secret source of power.<br /> I'd love to see a minor battle between the Realm and Lookshy accidentally crack it open.<br /> I'd love to see a mortal adventurer think they're looking an artifact that will make them rich, but instead release the Solars and exalt as the first of their number.<br /> I'd love to see a freak Wyld storm/incursion break it open by accident.<br /> I'd love to see an intentional Wyld incursion break it open because only the Solars ever brought the Fair Folk lord the challenge they've sought.<br /> <br /> I'd love to see <b>all </b>of these be the reason. But more than any of that, I'd love for it to never be mentioned again in a book, so that <b>any </b>of these <i>could</i> be the reason. Because every one of these creates interesting story hooks that haven't been published before. The Deathlord/Yozi thing has been done. Twice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:48:47-08:00","id":1056310,"title":"","content":"For something <b><i>completely different</i></b> what if we put a focus on 3e's approach to exaltation as a &quot;blessing from the Sun&quot; instead of a &quot;green lantern ring&quot;? What if they're not a bunch of shards that the Sidereals locked up in a box?<br /> <br /> I propose a new headcanon that the Sidereals did a great Working that locked away the Sun's power from Creation after convincing him to turn away from his Chosen. Perhaps they spend decades influencing the Sun, drawing attention in heaven toward the Solar's atrocities and acts of selfishness and hedonism, so that the Sun turned his face away from Creation. With his attention gone, the Sidereals Worked a way to block his power from continuing through Creation. Then in the modern age, the Sun turns his face back upon Creation for the first time and sees heroes, who just need the power to save the world. His attention breaks the Working of the Sidereals, returning his power back unto Creation, blessing those heroes he was so impressed by.<br /> <br /> There's a ton of handwavy in here, because I just thought this up during lunch. But it helps shift the focus away from &quot;shards of exaltation&quot; to &quot;the influence of The Unconquered Sun&quot; at least somewhat. Just a headcanon, but it might be my new default in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T14:13:21-08:00","id":1056315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056310#post1056310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For something <b><i>completely different</i></b> what if we put a focus on 3e's approach to exaltation as a &quot;blessing from the Sun&quot; instead of a &quot;green lantern ring&quot;? What if they're not a bunch of shards that the Sidereals locked up in a box?<br /> <br /> I propose a new headcanon that the Sidereals did a great Working that locked away the Sun's power from Creation after convincing him to turn away from his Chosen. Perhaps they spend decades influencing the Sun, drawing attention in heaven toward the Solar's atrocities and acts of selfishness and hedonism, so that the Sun turned his face away from Creation. With his attention gone, the Sidereals Worked a way to block his power from continuing through Creation. Then in the modern age, the Sun turns his face back upon Creation for the first time and sees heroes, who just need the power to save the world. His attention breaks the Working of the Sidereals, returning his power back unto Creation, blessing those heroes he was so impressed by.<br /> <br /> There's a ton of handwavy in here, because I just thought this up during lunch. But it helps shift the focus away from &quot;shards of exaltation&quot; to &quot;the influence of The Unconquered Sun&quot; at least somewhat. Just a headcanon, but it might be my new default in my games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like this almost infinitely better than the current (?) &quot;LOL, gonna lock up all your stuffs&quot;-shtick the background lore has going on. + + +","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T15:00:04-08:00","id":1056332,"title":"","content":"Unless I deem it necessary to change for a specific campaign, I'll probably stick to &quot;Deathlords and Yozi did it&quot;, but the actual operation will be vague (and crab-free). The forces of darkness, stealing the light of the sun to pervert to their own use is plenty mythic enough for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T15:19:42-08:00","id":1056339,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar368_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"368\" data-vbnamecard=\"368\">The Unsung Hero</a>, it's a cool idea, but I'm also jaded enough to know that in the hands of a skilled enough writer or speaker, a vast sorcerous construct of jade and iron, a physical representation of a prison that yet bound the immaterial and immanent gift of the Sun, would not invoke any &quot;Green Lantern Ring&quot; vibes. (While a mystical immaterial working would just turn to dross if not handled skillfully!).<br /> <br /> *Mind you anything's better than stealing that bloody cabinet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T16:49:41-08:00","id":1056374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056339#post1056339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar368_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"368\" data-vbnamecard=\"368\">The Unsung Hero</a>, it's a cool idea, but I'm also jaded enough to know that in the hands of a skilled enough writer or speaker, a vast sorcerous construct of jade and iron, a physical representation of a prison that yet bound the immaterial and immanent gift of the Sun, would not invoke any &quot;Green Lantern Ring&quot; vibes. (While a mystical immaterial working would just turn to dross if not handled skillfully!).<br /> <br /> *Mind you anything's better than stealing that bloody cabinet...</div> </div> </div> </div>It was more getting away from the idea of Exaltations being these sort of separate &quot;things&quot; exist on their own. When unbound, they go and seek out and worthy host that fits it's criteria and then bonds with them (hence the Green Lantern Ring comparison). The Jade Prison simply held all of these &quot;things&quot; in a very literal sense. That was the presentation in 2e. Whatever the construct that holds back the power, my idea was to get away from Exaltations being distinct &quot;things&quot; and go towards it being a direct blessing from the Sun. His power represented in Creation. That's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T18:09:03-08:00","id":1056397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056224#post1056224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not a single &quot;IT'S ME AUSTIN&quot; in three pages? For shame.<br /> <br /> Anyways, my position is &quot;Deathlords &amp; Yozis is likely but other explanations are not barred at this point&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was indeed the Deathlords &amp; Yozis, but they didn't use a crab.<br /> &lt;---------------------------------------<br /> They used a big green turtle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T20:39:17-08:00","id":1056451,"title":"","content":"This thread is the first time I've ever heard of the Jade Prison being broken by a giant crab monster.<br /> <br /> I knew it'd been broken, but what I knew of the setting (mostly stuff from KoC tbph) implied that The Ebon Dragon had a pretty heavy hand in the prison break (albeit not a direct one). My own headcanon had been that the Scarlet Empress' disappearance shortly before the return of the Solars was not a coincidence. Given that the Yozis and the Deathlords both got some of the Exaltations, and that TED (apparently?) married the Scarlet Empress, it seemed an open-and-shut case, from a narrative perspective. There was a conspiracy between the Yozis, the Neverborn/Deathlords (i kept mixing up which was which and for some reason thought the Deathlords only came into existence after the Prison was broken?) and the Scarlet Empress to release the Solars into the world again, and to bring half of them to the bad guys.<br /> <br /> Why? Good question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You tell me.<br /> <br /> I will continue to make that assumption because <b>ARE YOU KIDDING ME A F#@$ING GIANT CRAB WHY HOW WHAT WHAT DOES THAT EVEN HAVE TO DO WITH THE DEAD?!</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T00:05:13-08:00","id":1056511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056451#post1056451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will continue to make that assumption because <b>ARE YOU KIDDING ME A F#@$ING GIANT CRAB WHY HOW WHAT WHAT DOES THAT EVEN HAVE TO DO WITH THE DEAD?!</b></div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't <i>literally</i> a giant crab. It was some kind unknown of behemoth that the Deathlords modified.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MoEP: The Abyssals page 26</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To breach the Jade Prison, the Deathlords began with the monstrous, semi-preserved carcass of a behemoth they dredged from the depths of the Western Ocean. They equipped it with tremendous claws, an armored tail and eyes that could not only see in the black depths but report what they saw in perfect detail. Between its jaws, like baleen in a whale\u2019s mouth, the Deathlords fixed hundreds of spiked chains built from the designs the Yozis had provided as a show of good faith. The Deathlords animated this hideous monstrosity with mighty necromancy and sent it toward its target. It scudded along the bottom of the ocean and into the Inland Sea, where it found the Jade Prison</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T00:20:26-08:00","id":1056515,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar879_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"879\" data-vbnamecard=\"879\">HalfTangible</a> Well it was a zombie behemoth. I mean Anubis cites the specific description, but yeah it was dead, it was aquatic in nature, and it could be upgraded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T00:51:11-08:00","id":1056527,"title":"","content":"Actually looking at the description again, it doesn't sound all that much like a crab.<br /> <br /> Or particularly dumb, for that matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T01:19:35-08:00","id":1056531,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar368_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"368\" data-vbnamecard=\"368\">The Unsung Hero</a>, thanks I understand a bit better now. It seems like if you still have Exaltations with a consistent individual past life history, then it seems really hard still not to think of them as concrete indivisible &quot;things&quot; that pass from bearer to bearer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T02:21:37-08:00","id":1056542,"title":"","content":"That's easily fixed though. Instead of a single individual's memories, a new exalt gets a random selection of memories from a pool of <i>all</i> deceased solars. More recent ones being closer to the top. <br /> <br /> In the first age it would often seem like exaltations passed on wholesale because the solars tended to die one at a time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T02:57:01-08:00","id":1056558,"title":"","content":"I have to say, I'm mostly fine with the Deathlords being the culprits and the Yozis being the instigators, because there's delicious irony in these guys in particular releasing the Solars from their prison. We could probably make do with fewer details of how they accomplished it, though - just because the Deahlords are necromancers doesn't mean they have to solve all their problems by throwing zombies at them, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T07:03:05-08:00","id":1056619,"title":"","content":"I think it may be that Michael Goodwin did a lot to ruin &quot;evil is self-defeating and stupid&quot; for me, at least with regards to Exalted.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm all for the Deathlords having fallibility, but at this point my response to them being the incompetent architects of their own downfall is a bit cold; I'd prefer them to have a bit more credibility.<br /> <br /> \u200bOn the other hand, the idea that there's not really much of a grand destiny behind the return of the Solar Exalted, and that it could amount to a fortuitous accident... at the moment, it doesn't appeal to me personally so much as their return being an expression of the narrative of the entombed folk hero coming again at the hour of greatest need, but there's a nihilism to it that I can certainly see the appeal of for people who would want to play up that aspect of the setting.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt's at times like this that I hope the books would take a minimalistic approach to filling in certain aspects, to more readily accommodate alternative interpretations.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: As for the Jade Prison itself, I don't know if it's specifically a reference to the 108 Stars of Destiny having been imprisoned since time immemorial beneath an ancient stele-bearing stone tortoise, but... it probably has a source in common.<br /> <br /> \u200bHonestly, even apart from the fact that I don't quite come down on &quot;Exaltations are not literal things&quot; as hard as some other people to do, for me a case like this is one in which no level of abstraction can get the same kind of visceral thrill as the idea of some kind of ominous vessel.<br /> <br /> \u200bA sarcophagus, a tomb, a chest, a Han dynasty burial suit, whichever; there can be more to it than being an object, but the tactile nature of it is very endearing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-01-2017, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T07:46:27-08:00","id":1056634,"title":"","content":"I don't think this particular turn of events counts as a failure on the Deathlords' part. Whatever the details, releasing all Solar Exaltations from a prison meant to hold them forever and immediately recapturing half of them is no mean feat.<br /> <br /> I agree the Jade Prison works best as a physical vessel, but having the Deathlords simply crack it open with brute force feels anticlimactic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T08:39:36-08:00","id":1056648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firstaide</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055928#post1055928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thumbs up dude. I like this metaphorical prison much better than a physical one. Kudos.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem I have with this idea [snarkily described above as 'a literal Deathlord's actual master plan'] is twofold.<br /> <br /> 1) It implies a degree of complicity and malice to every Sidereal since the Usurpation I find nearly as bad as Lilun for Infernals. &quot;We have participated in steadily grinding out the light of humanity since time immemorial 'for its' own good', but for its' own good, we mean so we don't get in trouble when they come back.&quot; In some several thousand years there have been no malcontent Sidereals acting against this Grand Doctrine enough to cause more than one or two rogue Solars? Plus it implies, like, &quot;Check your humanity at the door&quot;, which I know is somehow really popular to assign to Sidereals but I find frankly ridiculous; the instant they get to Heaven they stop having personal biases and opinions on things? &quot;At least my suffering to this point was part of some master plan...&quot; &quot;Yeah it was basically so we didn't have to take down the Solars again.&quot; &quot;...What.&quot; &quot;Yeah, outside of that it's pretty meaningless, totally not necessary for Fate to function, just made our jobs easier.&quot; &quot;.......<i>what</i>.&quot;<br /> It changes the context of the Sidereal stance, from &quot;We ACCEPT that Creation will be lessened in exchange for its' salvation, but this is a cost we willingly bear the burden of on our shoulders&quot; to &quot;We MANDATE that Creation will be lessened in exchange for its' salvation, and we will be tasked forevermore with personally going around swinging wrenches at kneecaps, metaphorically speaking&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2) I know solar fanboys like to pretend Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals aren't REALLY Exalted, but even in 2e and I'm pretty sure even MORE so in 3e, there was still supposed to be the same sort of 'spark' of heroism, the moment that pushed them to rise up and ignite the dormant power in their blood or their stars......... which would be just as smothered by this grand master plan of ensuring noone rises up. Also, 3e is pushing away from &quot;And then I rose up and punched out the Dragon Blooded Satrap screaming WHAT THE CHRIST ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT&quot; as the default Solar Exaltation; Perfect Soul threw a hissy fit at a shrine of the Sun, Prince Diamond did a little legal wrangling and accepted punishment in his brother's place using an obscure law of his people, etc.<br /> <br /> I mean it works fine if you consider the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded and Lunars and Exigents not REALLY Exalted to the degree Solars are and the Sidereals to actually be the real villains of everything rather than misguided heroes who made a decision that was both unfortunate for Creation but the best option available to them, but I'm pretty sure neither of these tenets is accurate to the game as it stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 03-01-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T10:22:27-08:00","id":1056679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colognian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055339#post1055339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did the Jadeprison look like?<br /> <br /> What did the exaltations look live?<br /> (When they still were in the Jadeprison)</div> </div> </div> </div>Apparently it looked like a zerg hive where exaltations were kept in shiny oval egg-like objects. It also had a hallway where sidereal inspectors could walk and chat around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T10:37:00-08:00","id":1056686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Meianno Yuurei</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056648#post1056648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem I have with this idea [snarkily described above as 'a literal Deathlord's actual master plan'] is twofold.<br /> <br /> 1) It implies a degree of complicity and malice to every Sidereal since the Usurpation I find nearly as bad as Lilun for Infernals. &quot;We have participated in steadily grinding out the light of humanity since time immemorial 'for its' own good', but for its' own good, we mean so we don't get in trouble when they come back.&quot; In some several thousand years there have been no malcontent Sidereals acting against this Grand Doctrine enough to cause more than one or two rogue Solars? Plus it implies, like, &quot;Check your humanity at the door&quot;, which I know is somehow really popular to assign to Sidereals but I find frankly ridiculous; the instant they get to Heaven they stop having personal biases and opinions on things? &quot;At least my suffering to this point was part of some master plan...&quot; &quot;Yeah it was basically so we didn't have to take down the Solars again.&quot; &quot;...What.&quot; &quot;Yeah, outside of that it's pretty meaningless, totally not necessary for Fate to function, just made our jobs easier.&quot; &quot;.......<i>what</i>.&quot;<br /> It changes the context of the Sidereal stance, from &quot;We ACCEPT that Creation will be lessened in exchange for its' salvation, but this is a cost we willingly bear the burden of on our shoulders&quot; to &quot;We MANDATE that Creation will be lessened in exchange for its' salvation, and we will be tasked forevermore with personally going around swinging wrenches at kneecaps, metaphorically speaking&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2) I know solar fanboys like to pretend Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals aren't REALLY Exalted, but even in 2e and I'm pretty sure even MORE so in 3e, there was still supposed to be the same sort of 'spark' of heroism, the moment that pushed them to rise up and ignite the dormant power in their blood or their stars......... which would be just as smothered by this grand master plan of ensuring noone rises up. Also, 3e is pushing away from &quot;And then I rose up and punched out the Dragon Blooded Satrap screaming WHAT THE CHRIST ARE YOU TALKING ABOUT&quot; as the default Solar Exaltation; Perfect Soul threw a hissy fit at a shrine of the Sun, Prince Diamond did a little legal wrangling and accepted punishment in his brother's place using an obscure law of his people, etc.<br /> <br /> I mean it works fine if you consider the Sidereals and Dragon-Blooded and Lunars and Exigents not REALLY Exalted to the degree Solars are and the Sidereals to actually be the real villains of everything rather than misguided heroes who made a decision that was both unfortunate for Creation but the best option available to them, but I'm pretty sure neither of these tenets is accurate to the game as it stands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think that either 1 or 2 is necessarily true.<br /> <br /> My thoughts on the heroic spark is that there is a different form for each Exalted type; it's pretty easy to draw that conclusion when you look at how each Exalt is 'chosen' in vastly different ways and how it's reflected in their abilities (Lunars have to try when survival is impossible, and they're the tough adaptable survivors. Solars have to attempt the impossible and succeed, and they get Supernals. etc etc). For Sidereals, I see them as destined heroes. Their entire shtick is meant to be that they have a part to play in Creation, and their 'spark' is that they accept this truth and push to fulfill that part to play, as best as they can.<br /> <br /> While this doesn't necessarily imply the Sidereals are mindless, nor would I suggest that the Maidens have gone out of their way to choose people who would be complicit in this (though that's possible), it does imply trust in authority. A Sidereal's been brought up and made to believe that Fate has a grand plan, and that their role is to play their part to perfection. They run heaven and a bureaucracy, the latter of which reacts to change with hostility.<br /> <br /> A Sidereal's place is not to question, nor to act against their masters; it is to interpret the will of fate and do everything in their power to bring about the best path. Think Jedi.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean a Sidereal is necessarily a bad person, or that they think the Prison is a good thing. But they've been taught to trust the will of the force- I mean, Fate - all their lives, by every teacher they've ever had. Putting trust in Fate's plan is what gives them their power, it's what moves them up in the bureaucracy. Seeing what they do of Fate probably allows them to see what happens when one tries to defy it, and I don't think it's pretty<br /> <br /> And if they did rebel? I imagine they'd lose privileges and political power very quickly.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how I feel about a physical vs metaphorical prison persay, but I <b>do</b> think there should be a physical representation of it. (I've been picturing a floating orb that exploded when it was 'broken')","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#post10856903\" target=\"_blank\">GitP Forums</a><br /> Playing Peleps Raptor, Fire Aspect playboy in the Grand Tour","edited":{"userid":879,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","user":"HalfTangible","date":". 03-01-2017, 01:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/879-halftangible","name":"HalfTangible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar879_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T10:37:33-08:00","id":1056687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HalfTangible</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056451#post1056451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will continue to make that assumption because <b>ARE YOU KIDDING ME A F#@$ING GIANT CRAB WHY HOW WHAT WHAT DOES THAT EVEN HAVE TO DO WITH THE DEAD?!</b></div> </div> </div> </div> I may be a minority around here, but I'm kinda sick of death being represented only by &quot;vertebrate death&quot;. Want some necro minions? They all are skelletons!<br /> <br /> I think that it's creative to make necrotech with the exoskelleton of a death sea-creature. Sure it can seem dumb if we all imagine it as a giant crab making undead bubbles with his mouth. But I think it could be a massive mountainous machine made out from the remnants of an arthropod-like behemoth (check your local cambrian fauna for some wacky ideas) covered with tons of fossil coral remnants, ghost sponges filtering souls, and whatever. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:00:53-08:00","id":1056694,"title":"","content":"I'll admit, I kind of like the Solar Exaltations being locked away somewhere. I can see a few Sidereals going along with the Usurpation with the assurance that &quot;If something happens, we can always crack open the Jade Prison and release the Solars&quot;. <br /> <br /> Of course, no emergency was ever bad enough for Kejak to break the Jade Prison open.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:06:41-08:00","id":1056697,"title":"","content":"I like the idea that part of the Jade Prison is constructed out of the Broken Constellation of the Mask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:08:34-08:00","id":1056699,"title":"","content":"Brainstorm: what if the Jade Prison didnt hold the Exaltatuons as disembodied Essences? What if the Sidereals or whoever killed the original powerful Solars, then grabbed the reincarnated bearers as soon as they could (so they'd still be E1, so managable), and entrapped them in a comatose stasis. And someone &quot;freed&quot; them by shutting down life suppirt or otherwise killing them.<br /> <br /> removes Lytek's cabinet from the equation doing it this way. And maybe the shock of it somehow caused some to turn into or split* and become Abyssal Essence<br /> <br /> <br /> * I am rather partial to the idea of Abyssals being new or split off rather than converted Solars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 03-01-2017, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:14:04-08:00","id":1056702,"title":"","content":"That's a nifty idea, but it really would force me to make a handful of &quot;Prison Survivors&quot; that escaped.<br /> <br /> But its a cool idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:35:25-08:00","id":1056706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056694#post1056694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I kind of like the Solar Exaltations being locked away somewhere. I can see a few Sidereals going along with the Usurpation with the assurance that &quot;If something happens, we can always crack open the Jade Prison and release the Solars&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, no emergency was ever bad enough for Kejak to break the Jade Prison open.</div> </div> </div> </div>Including the Death of Nearly Everything, followed by The Fae Really Mean It This Time? Don't get me wrong; I like my Sids with a fair amount of hubris, but does that not risk making Kejak into a caricature?<br /> <br /> Anyway, after reading this thread, I've conclude it's best to not describe how the Solars were freed for one simple reason: everyone has different aesthetics. Undead Behemoth crab is cool to some people; squeezing the hope out of all humanity is cool to some people. It's probably best if the question isn't answered so we spend more time playing the game and less time taking pot shots at material that was written (in some cases) over a decade ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:38:09-08:00","id":1056708,"title":"","content":"Just an irk... it was a Hekatonhire in all likelyhood and not a Behemoth.<br /> <br /> And I like to Think Heaven would actually have stepped in if things got bad enough, and by that I mean all of Creation swept away up to the coasts of the Blessed Isle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T11:41:22-08:00","id":1056709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056706#post1056706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Including the Death of Nearly Everything, followed by The Fae Really Mean It This Time? Don't get me wrong; I like my Sids with a fair amount of hubris, but does that not risk making Kejak into a caricature?</div> </div> </div> </div>Creation is still here, isn't it?<br /> <br /> /Bronze Faction PoV<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:58:26-08:00","id":1056752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056702#post1056702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a nifty idea, but it really would force me to make a handful of &amp;quot;Prison Survivors&amp;quot; that escaped.</div> </div> </div> </div>You say that as though that's a bad thing.<br /> <br /> Go with it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:11:11-08:00","id":1056866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056694#post1056694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll admit, I kind of like the Solar Exaltations being locked away somewhere. I can see a few Sidereals going along with the Usurpation with the assurance that &quot;If something happens, we can always crack open the Jade Prison and release the Solars&quot;.<br /> <br /> Of course, no emergency was ever bad enough for Kejak to break the Jade Prison open.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bMy current notion is that the prison only worked because the Sun no longer supported the Solar Exalted, and whatever force was behind it opening, that could not have happened unless his will was with the idea that the Exalted should return.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt couples with the idea that the Sidereals were determined that nobody should ever find and open the thing again, so they just paddled around without navigation for a few days and dumped the thing in the ocean, then summoned the Calibration Gate. Made very sure that even they wouldn't know where they'd left it, and that it would be as impervious as possible to attempts to determine its location via divination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:27:07-08:00","id":1056915,"title":"","content":"Well I imagine the process for the Sids opening the Jade Prison would have been rather complicated and probably required a few people. I mean in fairness the Sids locked up the Solars under the presumption that the Solars were the biggest threat and the fact that this wasn't going to work twice. Cause sane person wouldn't want Godzilla getting loose just because some nut job showed up at the lock with a buzzsaw, plus they were going to need to make it so a rogue sid couldn't undue it.<br /> <br /> Of course the consequence of heavily sealing this thing and making it hard to find and open is that anything bad enough to necessitate opening the thing is also going to be straining the manpower and time of the Sidereal exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T19:18:07-08:00","id":1056935,"title":"","content":"Now I have an image of a Sidereal leafing through a book, and occasionally coming across a moving image of {insert appropriately humorous alteration of the name &quot;Edward Snowden&quot; to form more fitting to Exalted here} explaining how you can't make a form of the Jade Prison that could be easily opened by Heaven that would not also have the same opportunity present a high risk of compromise by the enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T22:41:23-08:00","id":1056992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056935#post1056935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now I have an image of a Sidereal leafing through a book, and occasionally coming across a moving image of {insert appropriately humorous alteration of the name &quot;Edward Snowden&quot; to form more fitting to Exalted here} explaining how you can't make a form of the Jade Prison that could be easily opened by Heaven that would not also have the same opportunity present a high risk of compromise by the enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maifa Millies Snowden?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Discord: HalfTangible#7505<br /> &quot;+3 Girlfriend is totally unoptimized. You are better off with a +1 Keen Witty girlfriend and then appling Greater Magic Make-up to increase her enhancement bonus.&quot; -Keld Danar on <a href=\"https://forums.giantitp.com/showthread.php?p=10856903#po