it ever existed and if it didn't survive very little reason to care.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T07:37:15-08:00","id":1057084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056708#post1056708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just an irk... it was a Hekatonhire in all likelyhood and not a Behemoth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per 2e description, it was a carcass of a sea behemoth animated by necromancy. Which is a different thing from a Hekatonkhire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T08:18:53-08:00","id":1057100,"title":"","content":"Aren't Hekatonkhires dead Behemoths?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T09:00:31-08:00","id":1057115,"title":"","content":"Hekatonkhire are ghost monsters some were behemoths, some were deva/demons and some were nightmares of the Neverborn given form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T09:12:28-08:00","id":1057119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1057084#post1057084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per 2e description, it was a carcass of a sea behemoth animated by necromancy. Which is a different thing from a Hekatonkhire.</div> </div> </div> </div>As pointed out that isn't really true. Some Hekatonhires are Dead Behemoths. So aren't. This thing isn't a living Behemoth so It would be a Hekatonhire, its more complex then rope pully skellyton.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T09:37:45-08:00","id":1057128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1057119#post1057119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As pointed out that isn't really true. Some Hekatonhires are Dead Behemoths. So aren't. This thing isn't a living Behemoth so It would be a Hekatonhire, its more complex then rope pully skellyton.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uh, no. Hekatonkhires may arise from slain Behemoths, but not all undead Behemoths are Hekatonkhires. If someone kills a Behemoth and it continues to exist as an undead abomination, it's a Hekatonkhire. If a necromancer finds a dead Behemoth and raises it with Necromancy, it's <i>not</i> a Hekatonkhire - it's a Behemoth zombie, or a necrotech construct if you prefer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T09:44:12-08:00","id":1057131,"title":"","content":"The Sheer Necromantic Puissiance I would argue means it would have to Hekatonhire rather then just a mobile fortress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T10:47:14-08:00","id":1057152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1057131#post1057131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sheer Necromantic Puissiance I would argue means it would have to Hekatonhire rather then just a mobile fortress.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing - the necromantic puissance used makes it <i>not a Hekatonkhire</i>, because Hekatonkhires can only be summoned by Necromancy, not created by it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T12:59:35-08:00","id":1057203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1057131#post1057131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sheer Necromantic Puissiance I would argue means it would have to Hekatonhire rather then just a mobile fortress.</div> </div> </div> </div>The creature used by the Deathlords was in essence, a really fancy zombie, just one using the corpse of a Behemoth instead of the corpse of a human. Hekatonkhire are more like really fancy ghosts, formed from the souls of slain Behemoths.<br /> <br /> Admittedly sometimes the lines can get blurry. For instance, while the Juggernaut is certainly an example of necromantic might and is animated through the power of Necromancy, it's not actually a corpse or a Hekatonkhire, but rather it's a still living behemoth. In the event that the Juggernaut actually dies, it's likely that the Mask of Winters will retain its corpse for use as a weapon while its soul moves on to to the Underworld to reform as a Hekatonkhire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T13:22:20-08:00","id":1057215,"title":"","content":"That's the thing they do straddle the line, and when it comes to things like behemoths, body and soul divide also straddles the line. So I'm saying the power required to animate colossal Behemoth transforms it from a Behemoth Corpse to a Zombie. No where does it say Hekatonhire have to be immaterial in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T13:49:33-08:00","id":1057231,"title":"","content":"Really the term Behemoth could use some work. It basically means Strange Thing The Primordials Made Or Came From The Wyld, which are two very different origins. Hekatonkhire descends from Greek meaning Hundred Handed for no good reason, and means basically Strange Thing From The Underworld. I'd rather either call them all behemoths or separate wyld ones from primordial-created ones with a different term. Either way, there should be a &quot;first found&quot; hekatonkhire that literally had 100 hands, because that's cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:40:58-08:00","id":1057259,"title":"","content":"My understanding was always that &quot;Behemoth&quot; meant &quot;weird thing that defies all other classification&quot; and Hekatonkhire meant &quot;weird dead thing that defies all other classification,&quot; but those categories may be too broad for useful taxonomy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T15:43:47-08:00","id":1057298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1057231#post1057231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really the term Behemoth could use some work. It basically means Strange Thing The Primordials Made Or Came From The Wyld, which are two very different origins. Hekatonkhire descends from Greek meaning Hundred Handed for no good reason, and means basically Strange Thing From The Underworld. I'd rather either call them all behemoths or separate wyld ones from primordial-created ones with a different term. Either way, there should be a &quot;first found&quot; hekatonkhire that literally had 100 hands, because that's cool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well the name isn't random, its a call back to Wraith the Oblivion and is mainly a really cool name with Mythologically evocative imagery. In Wraith they were Giant Ghost Monsters, often with mutations like multiple limbs. they were the step below Oncebornhood in evolution. Then Exalted took that because the creatures are very much like them, a step below Neverborn. In the Greek Myth Hekatonhires were one generation removed from the Primordial Gods of the universe, they were impossibly massive and banished to the Underworld, that sounds pretty close to Exalteds. Yeah it probably literally was something along the lines of the first Hekatonhires encountered were giants with a Hundred arms and a thousand eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T16:28:40-08:00","id":1057323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colognian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1055339#post1055339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What did the Jadeprison look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like a Chinese cricket box made of Jade<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://www.antiques-buyers-collection.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/Chinese-Cricket-Box-6-Medium.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What did the exaltations look live?<br /> (When they still were in the Jadeprison) </div> </div> </div>Like Tinkerbell in a live action Peter Pan play.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T17:04:12-08:00","id":1057343,"title":"","content":"What if the Unconquered Sun broke open the Jade Prison himself, and <u>deliberately gave </u>some of the Solar shards to the Neverborn/Yozis, in secret, for reasons known only to the Incarna?<br /> <br /> Couple possible reasons he might have done so:<ul><li>The first age Solars only began to truly succumb to the Great Curse once they had established unchallenged dominion over the world. The greatest heroes need equally great villains, lest they fall to villainy themselves.</li> <li>The Incarna are aware of <u>something</u> that will happen in the future, and the Chosen of both Hell and the Underworld would be needed to counter it.</li> <li>Possibly related to either or both of the above, it's actually something of a work/release program. The former primordial select their chosen at the behest of Heaven. In exchange, the Neverborn achieve a measure of catharsis through the Abyssals and approach Lethe, while the Yozis slowly earn a chance at parole.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>She/Her pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12975-zealot_vedas","name":"Zealot_Vedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12975_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T13:27:04-08:00","id":1057740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1056709#post1056709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Creation is still here, isn't it?<br /> <br /> /Bronze Faction PoV<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>LOL. Sidereal politics is early 21st-century Twitter/Fake News Wars. It all makes sense now!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid the Magnificent</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding was always that &quot;Behemoth&quot; meant &quot;weird thing that defies all other classification&quot; and Hekatonkhire meant &quot;weird dead thing that defies all other classification,&quot; but those categories may be too broad for useful taxonomy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also my understanding. I would argue these categories are useful for purposes of the game, where precisely cataloging something is secondary to defeating it/leveraging it to your advantage.<br /> <br /> When my PCs go up against my end-boss Sky Nommer, the Slightly Impolite, I want them to feel a sense of dread, awe, and curiosity of what could have created such a monstrosity, not an urge to flip open a book and try to shoe-horn it into some jargon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T13:40:01-08:00","id":1057749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1057740#post1057740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> LOL. Sidereal politics is early 21st-century Twitter/Fake News Wars. It all makes sense now!<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Don't laugh, but I have used Fox News tactics on my players before. Having NPCs talk in neat little soundbites works well to portray a manipulative character and to make them more memorable. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T14:26:12-08:00","id":1057766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1057740#post1057740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also my understanding. I would argue these categories are useful for purposes of the game, where precisely cataloging something is secondary to defeating it/leveraging it to your advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. From a mechanical perspective the difference can be fairly important. Hekatonkhire, as creatures of the Underworld are pretty much always going to be Creatures of Darkness, which could have some important mechanical effects. Likewise Hekatonkhire can be summoned and bound by Necromancers, whereas you can't do the same thing with Behemoths (if you're a powerful Necromancer I suppose that would be an excellent way to definitively prove whether something is a Hekatonkhire or not). <br /> <br /> But from a more &quot;in-game&quot; perspective, 99% of the time the difference between a Hekatonkhire and Behemoth is barely even academic, and if you see some horrific gibbering monster charging at you, it's unlikely anyone will sit around debating whether it's a Primordial forged Behemoth, a Wyld forged one, or a Hekatonkhire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T11:01:46-08:00","id":1058096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1057766#post1057766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah. From a mechanical perspective the difference can be fairly important. Hekatonkhire, as creatures of the Underworld are pretty much always going to be Creatures of Darkness, which could have some important mechanical effects. Likewise Hekatonkhire can be summoned and bound by Necromancers, whereas you can't do the same thing with Behemoths (if you're a powerful Necromancer I suppose that would be an excellent way to definitively prove whether something is a Hekatonkhire or not).<br /> <br /> But from a more &quot;in-game&quot; perspective, 99% of the time the difference between a Hekatonkhire and Behemoth is barely even academic, and if you see some horrific gibbering monster charging at you, it's unlikely anyone will sit around debating whether it's a Primordial forged Behemoth, a Wyld forged one, or a Hekatonkhire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. The whole reason Behemoths and Hekatonkhires exist in Exalted is to be unique monsters/plot hooks. The concept loses the magic if you start applying Monster Manual-style sub-types to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-04T15:50:49-08:00","id":1058181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1057749#post1057749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Don't laugh, but I have used Fox News tactics on my players before. Having NPCs talk in neat little soundbites works well to portray a manipulative character and to make them more memorable.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI wonder how close this would be to Cato the Elder constantly ending speeches (regardless of content or context) with &quot;Carthage must be destroyed&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T00:16:39-08:00","id":1058317,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/1055267-who-set-the-solars-free?p=1058181#post1058181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">Vie